			OSQL
	      ORACLE Visual SQL Query Tool

---------------------------------------------------------------
		Text Entry Key Bindings
---------------------------------------------------------------


  Key			Result
  ---			------

  <Backspace>		Delete text left of the cursor.

  <Delete>		Delete text right of the cursor.

  <Cntl-s>		Save text in the current save file.

  <Meta-Down>		Move forward in the previous command
  			buffer and insert text.

  <Meta-Up>		Move backward in the previous
  			command buffer and insert text.

  <Return>		Insert a newline in the text.
  
  <Shift-Return>		Execute the text in the ORACLE server.
  			(Same as hitting the "Execute SQL"
  			button.)

  <Shift-Delete>		Clear all text from the SQL text entry area.


  NOTE:

  Text selected using mouse button-1 will be replaced
  by newly typed key strokes.
  